int CountDigits(int n)
{
    if (n < 10) return 1;
    return 1 + CountDigits(n / 10);
}

Identify and correct the error that prevents this function terminating for positive n.
int SumTo(int n)
{
    if (n == 0) return 0;
    return n + SumTo(n + 1);
}

Write a recursive function in C# that returns 2 to the power n, for a non-negative integer n.

Compare recursion with iteration. Give two differences and one advantage of recursion for a suitable problem.
